{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Moab.</b> This one — who was not modest — stated explicitly 'from my father,' but the younger one called it by a clean expression, and received reward in the days of Moses, as it is said concerning the children of Ammon: ״אַל תִּתְגַּר בָּם״ (Deuteronomy 2) — as a general rule; but concerning Moab He warned only that he not wage war against them, but to harass them He permitted him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:34.104942716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}